          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em foliation
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a decomposition into
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            %em leaves
            of the foliation and one says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %em foliated by the leaves
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "," do
              %em regular foliation
            = succeed ";" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+foliation"} singular foliation
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/immersion"} immersed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            that locally can be expressed as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersion"} submersion
            (the projection to the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+leaves"} space of leaves
          %p
            Historically (as they were introduced in
            %a{:href => "#Ehresmann"} Ehresmann
            and
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Reeb"} Reeb
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as arising from subbundles of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \hookrightarrow T X
            that are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+distributions"} integrable distributions
            in the sense that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+fields"} vector fields
            that are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is again a section of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            as encoding a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equation"} differential equation
          %p
            Expressed in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Lie+theory"} higher Lie theory
            such an integrable distribution is a sub-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of this structure foliations of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are also equivalently encodes as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            whose space of objects is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbits"} orbits
            are the leaves of the foliation.
          %p
            Moreover, foliations are classified by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+cohomology"} Čech cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            with coefficients in a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groupoid"} topological groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haefliger+groupoid"} Haefliger groupoid
            = succeed "-theory." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+higher+differential+geometry"} motivation for higher differential geometry
          %p
            The Haefliger groupoids in fact classifies structures slightly more general than foliations:
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haefliger+structures"} Haefliger structures
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p There are several equivalent definitions of foliations.
          %h3#original_definition Original definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            be an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
            subsets
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_\alpha
            = succeed "," do
              %strong leaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi α
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M  = \cup_\alpha V_\alpha
          %p
            is called a
            %strong foliation
            if there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            by a collection of “special”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charts"} charts
            of the form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U, \phi)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi = (\phi_1,\ldots,\phi_n) : U \to \mathbb{R}^n
            such that for each “special” chart and each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            there is a number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\leq n
            = succeed "," do
              %em dimension of the foliation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_\alpha
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is one of the level sets, i.e. the solution of the system
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi const
                  %mo =
                  %mi const
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_r(x) = const = const(r,U,\alpha)
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\gt p
          %p
            If the manifold is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %em smooth foliation
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                foliation in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are in 1-1 correspondence with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+distributions"} integrable distributions
            of hyperplanes of dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h3#alternative_definitions Alternative definitions
          %p
            The following equivalent definitions and their relation are discussed for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#MoerdijkMrcun"}> IfLg, 1.2
            ).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong foliation atlas
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              and leaf-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\phi_i^{-1}: R^n \to X\}_i
              such that the transition functions are globally of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi_{i j} : (x,y) \mapsto (g_{i j}(x,y), h_{i j}(y))
            %p
              with respect to the canonical decomposition
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mi q
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n = \mathbb{R}^{n-q} \times \mathbb{R}^q
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi q
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi h
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi q
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{R}^n &amp;\stackrel{\phi_{i j}}{\to}&amp; \mathbb{R}^n &amp;&amp;
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{R}^q &amp;\stackrel{h_{i j}}{\to}&amp; \mathbb{R}^q
                    }
                    \\,.
          #FoliationAtlasByLocalSubmersions.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong foliation atlas
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              and leaf-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}_i
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              equipped with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersions"} submersions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ s_i \colon U_i \to \mathbb{R}^q \}
              such that there exists
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphisms"} diffeomorphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\gamma_{i j} \colon s_j(U_i \cap U_j) \to s_i(U_i \cap U_j)
            %p
              satisfying on each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \cap U_j
              the condition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi j
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    s_i = \gamma_{i j} \circ s_j
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Given a foliation atlas as in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FoliationAtlasByLocalSubmersions"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphisms"} diffeomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\gamma_{i j}\}_{i,j}
              satisfy the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              condition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\gamma_{i j} \circ \gamma_{j k} = \gamma_{i k}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is called the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haefliger+cocycle"} Haefliger cocycle
              of the foliation atlas.
          #AsIntegrableDistribution.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A smooth foliation of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is equivalently an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+distribution"} integrable distribution
              (or an integrable subbundle)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \hookrightarrow T X
          %h3#InTermsOfLieAlgebroidsAndLieGroupoids In terms of Lie algebroids and Lie groupoids
          %p
            Definition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AsIntegrableDistribution"}
            above is immediately reformulated equivalently as the following statement in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Lie+theory"} higher Lie theory
          #AsLieAlgebroidsWithInjectiveAnchor.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is equivalently a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anchor+map"} anchor map
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
              which under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+differentiation"} Lie differentiation
              give rise to Lie algebroids with injective anchors as in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AsLieAlgebroidsWithInjectiveAnchor"}
              are precisely those which are Morita-equivalent to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+groupoids"} étale groupoids
              (hence are the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation+groupoids"} foliation groupoids
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#CrainicMoerdijk"} Crainic-Moerdijk 00, theorem 1
          %p One says:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
              %strong integrates
              a given foliation, if it
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integrates
              the coresponding
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AsLieAlgebroidsWithInjectiveAnchor"}
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+foliation"} simple foliation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              of a manifold
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimpleFoliation"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersion"} submersion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_{\mathcal{D}} \;\colon\; X \to X/\mathcal{D}
            %p
              to the leaf space, that map itself is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
              of a Lie groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
              which integrates the foliation, which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi X
                      %munder
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi 𝒟
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{G}_\bullet
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    X \underset{X/\mathcal{D}}{\times} X
                    \\stackrel{\to}{\to}
                    X/\mathcal{D}
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              Among all Lie groupoids that integrate a given foliation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
              of a manifold
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy+groupoid"} holonomy groupoid
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Hol
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℱ
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hol(X,\mathcal{F})_\bullet
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy+groupoid"} monodromy groupoid
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Monod
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℱ
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Monod(X,\mathcal{F})_\bullet
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
              with (for simplicity)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
              source-fibers.
            %p Then there are maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hol
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Monod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℱ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mi 𝒢
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi hol
                          %mi G
                    %mi Hol
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    hol
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Monod(X,\mathcal{F})_\bullet
                    \\stackrel{g_{\mathcal{G}}}{\to}
                    \\mathcal{G}_\bullet
                    \\stackrel{hol_G}{\to}
                    Hol(X,\mathcal{F})
            %p
              which are surjective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphisms"} local diffeomorphisms
              and such that the composite is the holonomy morphism (…).
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CrainicMoerdijk"}> Crainic-Moerdijk 00, prop. 1
            ).
          %h3#of_higher_smooth_spaces Of higher smooth spaces
          %p
            One can consider the generalization of the notion of foliation of manifolds to foliations of structures in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation+of+a+Lie+algebroid"} foliation of a Lie algebroid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation+of+a+Lie+groupoid"} foliation of a Lie groupoid
          %h3#InCohesiveHigherGeometry In terms of differential cohesive higher geometry
          %p
            The following is a suggestion for an axiomatization of foliations in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            in the formalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
          %blockquote
            %p Under construction.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_notation Definition (Notation)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
              equipped with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            %p
              As usual, we write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∫
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo ♭
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo ♯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\int \dashv \flat \dashv \sharp)
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modalities"} modalities
              that defines the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊣
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊣
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sharp+modality"} sharp modality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Red
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi inf
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi inf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Red \dashv \int_{inf} \dashv \flat_{inf})
              for the adjoint triple of modalities that defines the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+modality"} reduction modality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊣
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊣
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+flat+modality"} infinitesimal flat modality
          %p
            Below we are going to axiomatize aspects of the traditional description of foliations by
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation+groupoids"} foliation groupoids
            as discussed
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#InTermsOfLieAlgebroidsAndLieGroupoids"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} groupoid objects
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
          #NotationForGroupoidObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_notation_for_groupoid_objects_and_atlases Definition (Notation for groupoid objects and atlases)
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giraud-Rezk-Lurie+axioms"} Giraud-Rezk-Lurie axioms
              we may think of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-epimorphism"} 1-epimorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_0 \to \mathcal{G}
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              as an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
              of the cohesive
              = succeed "-groupoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo ∈
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G} \in \mathbf{H}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object
              which we write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                    %mo ≔
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mo ×
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{G}_\bullet \coloneqq \mathcal{G}_0^{\times^{\bullet+1}_{\mathcal{G}}}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence we use notation where omitting the subscript decorationon a groupoid object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet \in \mathbf{H}^{\Delta^{op}}
              refers to its realization
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo →
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{G} \coloneqq {\underset{\rightarrow}{\lim}}_n \mathcal{G}_{n}
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\in \mathbf{H}
                    \\,.
          %p We have the following “geometricity” constraints on groupoid objects.
          #GeometricAndEtale.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              any morphism in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Y
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mi inf
                        %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi inf
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \stackrel{L(f)}{\to} Y \underset{\int_{inf} Y}{\times} \int_{inf} X
            %p
              for the canonical morphism induced by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality
              of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi inf
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_{inf}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+smooth+morphism"} formally smooth morphism
                  (or
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersion"} submersion
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(f)
                  is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-epimorphism"} 1-epimorphism
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphism"} formally étale morphism
                  (or
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(f)
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
            %p
              Now if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon \mathcal{G}_0 \to \mathcal{G}
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-epimorphism"} 1-epimorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
              for the cohesive
              = succeed "-groupoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒢
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object
              as in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NotationForGroupoidObjects"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
                  is an
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} geometric ∞-groupoid
                  if its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
                  is a
                  = succeed "/" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+smooth+morphism"} formally smooth morphism
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersion"} submersion
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
                  is an
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} étale ∞-groupoid
                  if its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
                  is a
                  = succeed "/" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphism"} formally étale morphism
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
          #FoliationInDifferentialCohesion.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation"} foliation
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D} \colon X \to X//\mathcal{D}
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              which is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-epimorphism"} 1-epimorphism
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+smooth+morphism"} formally smooth morphism
            %p
              Equivalently a foliation of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a map that exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
              for a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} geometric ∞-groupoid
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeometricAndEtale"}
            %p
              Given a foliation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              we say that the
              %strong leaf decomposition
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              induced by the foliation is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi LeafDec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo ♭
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi 𝒟
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    LeafDec(\mathcal{D})
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\flat(X//\mathcal{D}) \underset{X//\mathcal{D}}{\times} X
            %p in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi LeafDec
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝒟
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ι
                                  %mi 𝒟
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi 𝒟
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♭
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi 𝒟
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi 𝒟
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    LeafDec(\mathcal{D}) &amp;\stackrel{\iota_{\mathcal{D}}}{\to}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\mathcal{D}}}
                    \\\
                    \\flat (X//\mathcal{D}) &amp;\to&amp; X//\mathcal{D}
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the bottom map is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
          %p
            Now let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔾
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Grp
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G} \in Grp_2(\mathbf{H})
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+%E2%88%9E-group"} braided ∞-group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mn 2
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi flat
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔾
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^2_{cl} := \Omega^2_{flat}(-,\mathbb{G})
          %p
            for the corresponding coefficient object for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            forms of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔾
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-connections"} principal ∞-connections
            (as discussed there).
          #IsotropicFoliationsInDiffCohe.num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p Given a closed 2-form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega \;\colon\; X \to \Omega^2_{cl}
            %p
              a foliation of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              by
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotropic+submanifold"} isotropic subspaces
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation"} foliation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
