              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbits"} orbits
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy+groupoid"} holonomy groupoid
          .num_example
            %h6#example_10 Example
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
              has a canonical structure of a foliation whose leaves are its maximal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic
              submanifolds, called
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+leaves"} symplectic leaves
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#leaf_space Leaf space
          %p
            The set of components of a foliation is typically non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"}> Hausdorff
            , which is one of the motivations of the
            = succeed "-style" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"} Connes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometry"} noncommutative geometry
          %h3#classification Classification
          %p
            Folitation are classified by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haefliger+groupoid"} Haefliger groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haefliger+theorem"} Haefliger theorem
          %h3#characteristic_classes Characteristic classes
          %p
            There is a theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+classes"} characteristic classes
            for foliations. A most well known example is the
            %span.newWikiWord
              Godbillon-Vey characteristic class
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Godbillon-Vey+characteristic+class"} ?
            for codimension one foliations.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bott+connection"} Bott connection
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy+groupoid"}> holonomy groupoid
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy+groupoid"} monodromy groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+theorem+%28differential+topology%29"} Frobenius theorem (differential topology)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry+applied+to+plain+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry applied to plain differential geometry
          %h2#References References
          %p
            The notion of foliated manifolds was introduced in the 1950s, motivated from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+differential+equation"} partial differential equation
            theory, in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"}> Charles Ehresmann
                , …
            %li
              %p Reeb, …
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%89lie+Cartan"}> Élie Cartan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Sur l’intégration des équations différentiels completement intégrable
          %p Early discussion:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Robert Hermann,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the differential geometry of foliations
                %strong 72
                3 (1960) 445-457 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1970226"}> jstor:1970226
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Thurston"}> William Thurston
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The theory of foliations of codimension greater than one
                %strong 49
                (1974) 214-231 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/139581"}> eudml:139581
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02566730"} doi:10.1007/BF02566730
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Thurston"}> William Thurston
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Existence of codimension-one foliations
                %strong 104
                (1976) 249-268 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1971047"}> jstor:1971047
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1971047"} doi:10.2307/1971047
          %p
            and in relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+groups"} diffeomorphism groups
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Thurston"}> William Thurston
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Foliations and Groups of Diffeomorphisms
                %strong 80
                2 (1974) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://scispace.com/pdf/foliations-and-groups-of-diffeomorphisms-8ti01j3mau.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Thurston-FoliationsAndDiffeos.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sam+Nariman"}> Sam Nariman
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Foliations and diffeomorphism groups
                %strong 71
                11 (2024) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.04047"}> arXiv:2401.04047
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/noti3080"} doi:10.1090/noti3080
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/notices/202411/rnoti-p1471.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
          %ul
            %li#MoerdijkMrcun
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Janez+Mrcun"} Janez Mrcun
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+foliations+and+Lie+groupoids"} Introduction to foliations and Lie groupoids
                %strong 91
                (2003) &amp;lbrack;ISBN: 0-521-83197-0&amp;rbrack;
            %li#CrainicMoerdijk
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marius+Crainic"}> Marius Crainic
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                %em Foliation groupoids and their cyclic homology
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0003119"}> arXiv:math/0003119
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The corresponding
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+algebras"} groupoid algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
              , chapter 2, section 8 of:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noncommutative+Geometry"} Noncommutative Geometry
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foliation"} Foliation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Mathematics"}> Encyclopedia of Mathematics
                \:
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://eom.springer.de/F/f040740.htm"} Foliation
          %p A survey by Fuks in Russian Itogi:
          %ul
            %li
              Д. Б. Фукс,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Слоения
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 18
              %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/php/getFT.phtml?jrnid=inta&paperid=93&what=fullt&option_lang=rus"} pdf
          %p Cohomology of formal vector fields and characteristic classes of foliations were originally studied in the papers
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                D. B. Fuks,
                %em Cohomology of infinite-dimensional Lie algebras and characteristic classes of foliations
                (book, Rus. and Eng. versions)
            %li
              %p
                I. M. Gelʹfand, B. L. Feĭgin, D. B. Fuks,
                %em
                  Cohomology of the Lie algebra of formal vector fields with coefficients in its dual space and variations of characteristic classes of foliations, Funkcional. Anal. i Priložen. 8 (1974), no. 2, 13–29 (Russian original
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/php/archive.phtml?wshow=paper&jrnid=faa&paperid=2326&option_lang=eng"} mathnet.ru
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/php/getFT.phtml?jrnid=faa&paperid=2326&volume=8&year=1974&issue=2&fpage=13&what=fullt&option_lang=eng"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Claude Godbillon,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cohomologies d’algèbres de Lie de champs de vecteurs formels
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 383
            %li
              %p
                И. М. Гельфанд, Д. Б. Фукс,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Когомологии алгебры Ли формальных векторных полей
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 34
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/php/getFT.phtml?jrnid=im&paperid=2418&what=fullt&option_lang=rus"} pdf
          %p In a series of works of Connes and Moscovici, the local index formulas in the context of transverse geometry of foliations has been studied in connection to a new cyclic homology of a Hopf algebra arising in this context:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+Connes"}> A. Connes
              , H. Moscovici,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Modular Hecke algebras and their Hopf symmetry
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0301089"} math.QA/0301089
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/distribution/mmj/vol4-1-2004/connes_moscovici_1.pdf"} ams
              = succeed "," do
                %em Hopf algebras, cyclic cohomology and the transverse index theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9806109"} math.DG/9806109
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 198
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1657389"} MR99m:58186
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s002200050477"} doi
              = succeed "," do
                %em Rankin-Cohen brackets and the Hopf algebra of transverse geometry
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differentiable cyclic cohomology and Hopf algebraic structures in transverse geometry
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 38
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1929328"} MR2003k:58042
            %li
              A. Connes,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Cyclic cohomology and the transverse fundamental class of a foliation
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 123
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=866491"} MR88k:58149
          %p More general issues of index theory in noncommutative geometry applied to foliations is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Yu. A. Kordyukov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Noncommutative geometry of foliations
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2456103"} MR2009m:58018
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Index theory and non-commutative geometry on foliated manifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Формула следов для трансверсально-эллиптических операторов на римановых слоениях
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/php/getFT.phtml?jrnid=aa&paperid=1108&what=fullt&option_lang=rus"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                W. P. Thurston,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Existence of codimension-one foliations
                %strong 104
                (1976), no. 2, 249–268 (
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BF02566730"}> doi
                );
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Foliations and groups of diffeomorphisms
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/bull/1974-80-02/S0002-9904-1974-13475-0/S0002-9904-1974-13475-0.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The theory of foliations of codimension greater than one
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://resolver.sub.uni-goettingen.de/purl?GDZPPN00206135X"} link
          %p
            The first of a series on foliations in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriele+Vezzosi"} Gabriele Vezzosi
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic foliations and derived geometry: the Riemann-Hilbert correspondence
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.05450"} arXiv:2001.05450
        .revisedby
